<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izeh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Idhaj, Malamir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izeh is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros Mountains</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> province, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> as Idhaj, it was the capital of the Hazaraspid dynasty of Greater Luristan from the 12th to the 15th century. Its surroundings contain Elamite rock reliefs at Kul-e Farah and Eshkaft-e Salman.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/izeh.jpg" alt="Izeh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pentocelo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kul-e_Farah_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
